== Structure ==

name_of_selector = {
	
	valid_character = { trigger } # which pool characters are valid to be considered
	character_score = { mtth } # score for random selection of valid pool characters
	config = {
		background = character_background # also used to validate pool characters (ie no need to check for trait that will be required by the background)
		age = { min max } # age span for randomization
	}
	
	selection_count = x # starting from the highest scoring candidates, the number of candidates that will be considered for random scoring (not scripting or setting to negative will use all valid =1 will select the highest scoring always (random tiebreaker )

	pool = faith/heritage # which character pool to search. faith = pool characters of scope:base's faith, heritage = pool characters of the heritage of the culture picked by 'culture'. Default faith
	court = yes/no # also include the courtiers of scope:base's court owner as candidates. Default no
	gender = random/male/female/clergy/commander/gender_law # gender of generated characters when no pool character is found. clergy = scope:base's rite clergy gender rules, commander = always male, gender_law = based on the gender law passed in by the code (male if none). Default random
	culture = character/province/company # culture of generated characters (and heritage for pool = heritage). character = scope:base's culture, province = culture of scope:province (falls back to character), company = culture of scope:base's primary title's mercenary company (falls back to character). Default character
}

Candidates are pool characters matching config.background, valid_character and with character_score > 0. If no candidate is found, a new character is generated using config, gender and culture.

Scopes that are always set:
root # the candidate pool character being evaluated (valid_character, character_score)
scope:base # the character that is set as the base character, usually the council owner or the predecessor

For the following hard-coded generators we also have additional scopes.

auto_generated_title_holder, auto_generated_local_title_holder, pool_theocratic_succession (used when generating a holder for a granted title; scope:base is the new liege) additional scopes:
scope:province # the province of the title that needs a generated holder (only set if the title has a province)
